      },
      "body": "With comms profiling on (`prof_all`, `prof` or `prof_ops`), the first `dist.all_gather_object(...)` or `dist.monitored_barrier()` prints `wrong comm_op specified` and ends the process with exit status 0, so a run stops silently.\n\n**Cause:** both ops are wrapped in `@timed_op`, but `calc_bw_log` has no branch for them and its fallback calls `exit(0)`.\n\n**Fix:** count `all_gather_object` with `all_gather` and `monitored_barrier` with the barrier ops. Their message size is 0, so bandwidth reads 0, as for `broadcast_object_list`.\n\n**Test:** `pytest tests/unit/comm/test_comms_logger.py` on CPU (gloo, macOS, no GPU): the new `supports_every_timed_op` case fails before (2 failed, `SystemExit: 0`), whole file passes after (54 passed). A gloo run with `prof_all` reproduced the exit before and logs both ops after.\n\nRelated open PRs #8695, #8795 and #8798 touch nearby logger code; none cover these two ops.\n",
